# Trivy ignore file — SCOPED to the compose-pulled third-party PostgreSQL image.
# It is passed via the `trivyignores:` input on exactly that scan step in
# .github/workflows/security.yml; repository-built backend/frontend/edge scans
# never load it, so our own images must stay at zero
# fixable HIGH/CRITICAL with no masking.
#
# Rationale for every entry: the fix exists upstream (a Debian point release
# or a rebuilt upstream binary), but the digest-pinned official
# image predates it and Docker Hub has not published a rebuilt tag. Compose
# service runs this image as-is, so there is no build step where an
# `apt upgrade` could apply the fix (the way our own Dockerfiles do).
#
# REFRESH POLICY: on each weekly security scan, re-check whether the pinned
# digests have been republished (Docker Hub tag last_updated) or newer
# stable tags exist, refresh them, and delete any entry whose CVE no longer
# appears. Never add entries for images this repository builds itself.
# The marker below is enforced by
# backend/scripts/check_trivy_ignore_freshness.py in CI (L-5, 2026-09-20
# audit): CI fails once it is more than 30 days old, so the acknowledged-CVE
# debt stays bounded instead of accumulating forever. Update it in the SAME
# change that refreshes the digests — never on its own.
